Well, I finally got around to checking this.  And yes, it looks like
there's an off-by-one bug in eating food.

Each food has a "delay" value which is how many turns it takes to eat
that food.  To eat a piece of food, nethack divides the food into
"bites", which is the amount of food consumed per turn.  The bug is
that if eating takes more than one turn, it stops one bite too early.
So a lembas which is 800nut/2turns ends up giving you 400nut, while a
food ration at 800nut/5turns gives you 600nut.  I'm pretty sure this
isn't what was intended.
